{"sections":[],"metadata":{"title":"Working with GeoJSON Data","modules":[{"name":"MapLibre"}],"roleHeading":"Article","role":"article"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre"]]},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/maplibre-native-for-ios\/geojson"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"occ"}]}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"anchor":"Adding-a-GeoJSON-file-to-the-map","type":"heading","text":"Adding a GeoJSON file to the map","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"MapLibre iOS offers several ways to work with "},{"identifier":"http:\/\/geojson.org\/","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" files."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"GeoJSON is a standard file format for representing geographic data."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"You can host a GeoJSON file or bundle it with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"your application, you can use a GeoJSON file as the basis of an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MLNShapeSource"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"object. Pass the file’s URL into the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MLNShapeSource\/initWithIdentifier:URL:options:"},{"type":"text","text":" initializer and add the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"shape source to the map using the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MLNStyle\/addSource:"},{"type":"text","text":" method. The URL may"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"be a local file URL, an HTTP URL, or an HTTPS URL."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Once you’ve added the GeoJSON file to the map via an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MLNShapeSource"},{"type":"text","text":" object,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"you can configure the appearance of its data and control what data is visible"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"using "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MLNStyleLayer"},{"type":"text","text":" objects. You can also"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"identifier":"#Extracting-GeoJSON-data-from-the-map","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Converting-GeoJSON-data-into-shape-objects","type":"heading","text":"Converting GeoJSON data into shape objects","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"If you have GeoJSON data in the form of source code (also known as “GeoJSON"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"text”), you can convert it into an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MLNShape"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MLNFeature"},{"type":"text","text":", or"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MLNShapeCollectionFeature"},{"type":"text","text":" object that the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MLNShapeSource"},{"type":"text","text":" class understands"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"natively. First, create an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NSData"},{"type":"text","text":" object out of the source code string or file"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"contents, then pass that data object into the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MLNShape\/shapeWithData:encoding:error:"},{"type":"text","text":" method. Finally, you can pass the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"resulting shape or feature object into the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MLNShapeSource\/initWithIdentifier:shape:options:"},{"type":"text","text":" initializer and add it to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the map, or you can use the object and its properties to power non-map-related"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"functionality in your application."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"To include multiple shapes in the source, create and pass an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MLNShapeCollection"},{"type":"text","text":" or"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MLNShapeCollectionFeature"},{"type":"text","text":" object to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MLNShapeSource\/initWithIdentifier:shape:options:"},{"type":"text","text":". Alternatively, use the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MLNShapeSource\/initWithIdentifier:features:options:"},{"type":"text","text":" or"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MLNShapeSource\/initWithIdentifier:shapes:options:"},{"type":"text","text":" method to create a shape source"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"with an array. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MLNShapeSource\/initWithIdentifier:features:options:"},{"type":"text","text":" accepts only "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MLNFeature"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"instances, such as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MLNPointFeature"},{"type":"text","text":" objects, whose attributes you can use when"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"applying a predicate to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MLNVectorStyleLayer"},{"type":"text","text":" or configuring a style layer’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"appearance."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Extracting-GeoJSON-data-from-the-map","type":"heading","text":"Extracting GeoJSON data from the map","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Any "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MLNShape"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MLNFeature"},{"type":"text","text":", or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MLNShapeCollectionFeature"},{"type":"text","text":" object has an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MLNShape\/geoJSONDataUsingEncoding:"},{"type":"text","text":" method that you can use to create a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"GeoJSON source code representation of the object. You can extract a feature"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"object from the map using a method such as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MLNMapView\/visibleFeaturesAtPoint:"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"About-GeoJSON-deserialization","type":"heading","text":"About GeoJSON deserialization","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The process of converting GeoJSON text into "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MLNShape"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MLNFeature"},{"type":"text","text":", or"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MLNShapeCollectionFeature"},{"type":"text","text":" objects is known as “GeoJSON deserialization”."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"GeoJSON geometries, features, and feature collections are known in this SDK as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"shapes, features, and shape collection features, respectively."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each GeoJSON object type corresponds to a type provided by either this SDK or"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the Core Location framework:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"header":"row","rows":[[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"GeoJSON object type"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"SDK type"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Position"},{"type":"text","text":" (longitude, latitude)"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"CLLocationCoordinate2D"},{"type":"text","text":" (latitude, longitude)"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Point"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MLNPointAnnotation"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MultiPoint"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MLNPointCollection"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"LineString"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MLNPolyline"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MultiLineString"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MLNMultiPolyline"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Polygon"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MLNPolygon"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MultiPolygon"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MLNMultiPolygon"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GeometryCollection"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MLNShapeCollection"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Feature"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MLNFeature"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"FeatureCollection"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MLNShapeCollectionFeature"}]}]]],"type":"table"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Feature"},{"type":"text","text":" object in GeoJSON corresponds to an instance of an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MLNShape"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"subclass conforming to the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MLNFeature"},{"type":"text","text":" protocol. There is a distinct"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MLNFeature"},{"type":"text","text":"-conforming class for each type of geometry that a GeoJSON feature"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"can contain. This allows features to be used as raw shapes where convenient. For"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"example, some features can be added to a map view as annotations. Note that"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"identifiers and attributes will not be available for feature querying when a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"feature is used as an annotation."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"In contrast to the GeoJSON standard, it is possible for "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MLNShape"},{"type":"text","text":" subclasses"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"other than "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MLNPointAnnotation"},{"type":"text","text":" to straddle the antimeridian."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The following GeoJSON data types correspond straightforwardly to Foundation data"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"types when they occur as feature identifiers or property values:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"header":"row","rows":[[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"GeoJSON data type"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Objective-C representation"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Swift representation"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"null"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NSNull"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NSNull"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"true"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"false"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NSNumber.boolValue"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Bool"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Integer"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NSNumber.unsignedLongLongValue"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NSNumber.longLongValue"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"UInt64"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Int64"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Floating-point number"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NSNumber.doubleValue"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Double"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"String"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NSString"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"String"}]}]]],"type":"table"}],"kind":"content"}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Styling and Dynamic Data","anchor":"Styling-and-Dynamic-Data","identifiers":["doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre-Native-for-iOS\/AnimatedLineExample","doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre-Native-for-iOS\/WebAPIDataExample","doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre-Native-for-iOS\/LineStyleLayerExample","doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre-Native-for-iOS\/DDSCircleLayerExample","doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre-Native-for-iOS\/POIAlongRouteExample","doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre-Native-for-iOS\/PMTiles"],"generated":true}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre-Native-for-iOS\/GeoJSON","interfaceLanguage":"occ"},"kind":"article","references":{"doc://org.swift.MyProject/documentation/MapLibre-Native-for-iOS/PMTiles":{"kind":"article","url":"\/documentation\/maplibre-native-for-ios\/pmtiles","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Working with PMTiles"}],"title":"PMTiles","identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre-Native-for-iOS\/PMTiles","role":"article","type":"topic"},"http://geojson.org/":{"identifier":"http:\/\/geojson.org\/","type":"link","title":"GeoJSON","titleInlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"GeoJSON"}],"url":"http:\/\/geojson.org\/"},"doc://org.swift.MyProject/documentation/MapLibre-Native-for-iOS/POIAlongRouteExample":{"kind":"article","url":"\/documentation\/maplibre-native-for-ios\/poialongrouteexample","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Use an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NSPredicate"},{"type":"text","text":" to show POI and road labels along a route."}],"title":"POI Along a Route","identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre-Native-for-iOS\/POIAlongRouteExample","role":"article","type":"topic"},"doc://org.swift.MyProject/documentation/MapLibre":{"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/maplibre","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Powerful, free and open-source mapping toolkit with full control over data sources and styling."}],"title":"MapLibre","identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre","role":"collection","type":"topic"},"doc://org.swift.MyProject/documentation/MapLibre/MLNLineStyleLayer":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNLineStyleLayer","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" is a style layer that renders one or more stroked"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"polylines on the map."}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNLineStyleLayer","fragments":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MLNLineStyleLayer"}],"title":"MLNLineStyleLayer","url":"\/documentation\/maplibre\/mlnlinestylelayer","type":"topic","role":"symbol"},"#Extracting-GeoJSON-data-from-the-map":{"identifier":"#Extracting-GeoJSON-data-from-the-map","type":"link","title":"access the data programmatically","titleInlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"access the data programmatically"}],"url":"#Extracting-GeoJSON-data-from-the-map"},"doc://org.swift.MyProject/documentation/MapLibre-Native-for-iOS/WebAPIDataExample":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Showing data from an API with custom styling and interaction"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre-Native-for-iOS\/WebAPIDataExample","kind":"article","type":"topic","title":"Showing data from an API","url":"\/documentation\/maplibre-native-for-ios\/webapidataexample","role":"article"},"doc://org.swift.MyProject/documentation/MapLibre-Native-for-iOS/AnimatedLineExample":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Add an animated line to a map"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre-Native-for-iOS\/AnimatedLineExample","kind":"article","type":"topic","title":"Animated Line","url":"\/documentation\/maplibre-native-for-ios\/animatedlineexample","role":"article"},"doc://org.swift.MyProject/documentation/MapLibre-Native-for-iOS/DDSCircleLayerExample":{"kind":"article","url":"\/documentation\/maplibre-native-for-ios\/ddscirclelayerexample","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Add and style a vector tile source"}],"title":"Vector Tile Sources","identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre-Native-for-iOS\/DDSCircleLayerExample","role":"article","type":"topic"},"doc://org.swift.MyProject/documentation/MapLibre-Native-for-iOS/LineStyleLayerExample":{"kind":"article","url":"\/documentation\/maplibre-native-for-ios\/linestylelayerexample","abstract":[{"text":"Adding an ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNLineStyleLayer","type":"reference"},{"text":" to the map using a GeoJSON file.","type":"text"}],"title":"Using GeoJSON with a line style layer","identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre-Native-for-iOS\/LineStyleLayerExample","role":"article","type":"topic"}}}